      <div class="card">
        <h3>The school day</h3>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row">School office opens</th><td>7:35 AM</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">School begins</th><td>{{ site.schoolDay.start }}</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Elementary dismissal (K5&ndash;5)</th><td>{{ site.schoolDay.elementaryEnd }}</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Secondary dismissal (6&ndash;12)</th><td>{{ site.schoolDay.secondaryEnd }}</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">All students picked up by</th><td>3:25 PM</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Office closes</th><td>3:30 PM</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="card__meta">The school cannot assume responsibility for students arriving before 7:35 AM</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>If school closes</h3>
        <p>When school closes for weather or another emergency, check in this order:</p>
        <ol class="list-tight">
          <li>Email and text through Schoolcast</li>
          <li>The school Facebook page and this website</li>
          <li>Your child's teacher</li>
          <li>Mr. Horn, (832) 294-1921 — only after the first three</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Reports and conferences</h3>
        <p>Weekly folders go home showing progress. Progress reports come four and a half weeks into each nine weeks; report cards at the end of each nine weeks. Both must be signed and returned the next day.</p>
        <p>The parent&ndash;teacher conference after the first nine weeks is required for all parents — that is when the report card is picked up.</p>
        <p><a href="/academics/grading/">Grading and reporting &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Talking to a teacher</h3>
        <p>Schedule conferences through the office, in advance. Teachers cannot discuss concerns while classes are in session, while on parking lot duty, or at church service times.</p>
        <p><a href="/about/faculty/">Faculty &amp; staff &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Lunch</h3>
        <p>Students bring their own lunches. If a student arrives without one, the school provides a lunch and charges it to the family account. Microwaves and refrigerators are not available to students.</p>
        <p>Parents are welcome to eat lunch with their child and may bring outside food when they do.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Dress code</h3>
        <p>Uniform items come from the French Toast website, using the stock numbers posted by the school. Shirts are white, grey or burgundy.</p>
        <p><a href="/student-life/dress-code/">Full dress code &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>

    </div>

